+### Trusted setup status
+
+**The trusted setup shipped in this repository is a demo setup in both phases.
+It is not a ceremony, and no security claim rests on it.** We say this up front
+rather than waiting to be asked.
+
+Groth16 needs a two-phase setup. Both halves here are development quality:
+
+| Phase | What was used | Standing |
+|---|---|---|
+| Phase 1 (universal) | Not a published ceremony. The key's alpha and beta match none, so the tau was generated locally — consistent with `circuits/payment-prover/README.md`, whose procedure starts `snarkjs powersoftau new bn128 14`. | **Demo only.** |
+| Phase 2 (circuit-specific) | One contribution, named `aperture-mpp-1777587329`, with no beacon. | **Demo only.** |
+
+A phase-2 setup is sound as long as at least one contributor destroyed their
+toxic waste. One contribution and no beacon reduces that to a single machine. A
+locally generated phase 1 collapses the same way one stage earlier: whoever ran
+`powersoftau new` held tau.
+
+Either half on its own is enough. Whoever held that entropy can forge a proof
+for **any** statement, including `is_compliant = 1` on a payment that violates
+the policy. The proofs still verify and the circuit still enforces what it says
+it enforces — but the soundness of the deployment rests on one party, not on
+nobody.
+
+Check the shipped artifact yourself:
+
+```bash
+node ../square/circuits/scripts/inspect-zkey-setup.mjs services/prover-service/artifacts/payment.zkey
+# phase-1 ceremony         UNRECOGNISED
+# phase-2 contributions    1
+# beacon applied           no
+```
+
+The tool reads both phases out of the zkey binary. Phase 1 is identified by
+`vk_alpha_1` and `vk_beta_2`, which snarkjs copies from the ptau and phase-2
+contributions never touch, making them a fingerprint of the tau. It lives in the
+[square](https://github.com/wienerlabs/square) repository, checked out beside
+this one.
+
+A public multi-party ceremony covering **both** phases is planned: an external,
+hash-verified powers of tau for phase 1, then contributions collected in the
+open with a beacon whose source is announced in advance, and published
+transcripts anyone can replay. Refreshing phase 2 alone would leave the key
+standing on a tau one machine produced. Until that lands, this setup is
+described as a demo everywhere it is mentioned.
+
 ### Why Circom + snarkjs
 
 Circom + snarkjs Groth16 is the only ZK stack that targets BN254 natively, has on-chain verification primitives in Solana mainline (`alt_bn128_*` syscalls + groth16-solana), produces proofs small enough to submit in a single Solana transaction, and proves fast enough on commodity CPUs to run inside an HTTP service. Aperture previously evaluated zkVM stacks; the trade off (multi-second proving, ~250 KB receipts, additional verifier router contracts) was not justified for a payment-gating circuit of this size.
